def _hex_to_bytes(hex_id):
    if len(hex_id) <= 16:
        int_id = unsigned_hex_to_signed_int(hex_id)
        return struct.pack('>q', int_id)
    else:
        high_id = unsigned_hex_to_signed_int(hex_id[:-16])
        high_bin = struct.pack('>q', high_id)
        low_id = unsigned_hex_to_signed_int(hex_id[-16:])
        low_bin = struct.pack('>q', low_id)
        return high_bin + low_bin


This function converts a hexadecimal string to a byte string. If the hexadecimal string is 16 characters or less, it directly converts the string to a signed integer and packs it into a 64-bit big-endian format. If the string is longer than 16 characters, it splits the string into two parts, each 16 characters long, converts each part to a signed integer, packs each part into a 64-bit big-endian format, and then concatenates the two byte strings.

